WEBVTT

01:27.140 --> 01:29.980
<b>AQUARION</b>

01:48.010 --> 01:50.740
<i>The Elements' mana gauge 
is rapidly dropping.</i>

01:52.330 --> 01:53.480
What is this?

01:56.920 --> 02:00.500
<i>Aquarion's emotional energy 
is undergoing phase reversal.</i>

02:01.000 --> 02:04.420
<i>The mana gauge has dropped even 
further. Now below threshold.</i>

02:04.820 --> 02:07.730
Their emotional waves are 
starting to dissipate!

02:07.940 --> 02:10.280
This is bad! They'll be torn apart!

02:18.410 --> 02:19.920
Guys, are you okay?

02:19.920 --> 02:20.490
Yeah.

02:20.910 --> 02:22.200
<i>Let's chase after it.</i>

02:24.720 --> 02:26.500
<i>Ah! It won't move!</i>

02:26.500 --> 02:27.720
Rimiya-kun!

02:29.690 --> 02:30.960
Is it going to...

02:30.960 --> 02:36.060
<i>Vector Tir Element's mana is decreasing. 
Unable to continue battle.</i>

02:36.060 --> 02:37.830
<i>The Mythic Beast isn't stopping!</i>

02:37.830 --> 02:40.270
<i>It's going to plant a stake!</i>

02:40.880 --> 02:42.020
Rimiya-kun!

02:43.400 --> 02:45.270
Y-Yes.

02:45.270 --> 02:47.930
Sakko, we've both got to help Rimiya-kun!

02:47.930 --> 02:49.120
<i>Got it!</i>

02:56.890 --> 02:58.140
<i>Don't let it plant that stake!</i>

02:58.400 --> 02:59.970
<i>What do you mean, stake?</i>

02:59.970 --> 03:01.200
<i>We won't!</i>

03:15.590 --> 03:16.450
<i>Oh, no!</i>

03:22.730 --> 03:23.930
They couldn't stop it.

03:24.420 --> 03:26.260
DEAVA is furious.

03:26.690 --> 03:29.270
Place a 500-meter radius 
blockade around the stake!

03:51.780 --> 03:53.790
<i>Rimiya-kun, are you okay?</i>

03:53.790 --> 03:55.010
<i>Rimiya!</i>

04:06.350 --> 04:10.320
Why did the Mythic Beast 
leave without a fight?

04:10.320 --> 04:13.310
Probably because once it planted a 
stake, it had completed its task.

04:13.910 --> 04:16.070
What is that stake thing anyway?

04:16.610 --> 04:18.750
The stakes create an enemy foothold.

04:18.750 --> 04:22.600
They entangle the area in mythic space 
to make it easier to open rifts.

04:22.980 --> 04:24.780
Quantum entanglement?

04:24.970 --> 04:28.480
Yeah. It's pretty much like 
a kind of domination battle.

04:28.690 --> 04:32.280
If there's just one stake, you can 
just blockade the area around it,

04:32.280 --> 04:37.650
but if the enemy places three down to form a
 triangle, that area becomes their territory.

04:38.200 --> 04:40.510
Like in the Bermuda Triangle 
in the Sargasso Sea,

04:40.510 --> 04:42.580
the Queimada Grande or "Snake Island,"

04:42.580 --> 04:44.580
or Area 51,

04:45.270 --> 04:50.950
you will find such blockaded areas inside 
forbidden regions around the world.

04:50.950 --> 04:54.860
That's how the Space Preservation 
Agency preserves them.

04:55.370 --> 05:00.790
When the stakes need to be within 
15 kilometers of each other to be effective.

05:02.750 --> 05:06.350
We can expect Mythic Beasts to 
appear again near that area.

05:08.430 --> 05:12.660
Fight off the Mythic Beasts, 
don't let them plant stakes...

05:12.660 --> 05:16.400
They keep dropping this stuff on us, 
but none of it makes any sense.

05:16.400 --> 05:21.130
Protecting the universe is way beyond 
our abilities to begin with.

05:21.130 --> 05:24.380
And something about this time was different.

05:24.380 --> 05:25.360
What do you mean?

05:26.040 --> 05:30.420
The feeling when we united. 
It wasn't like the first time we did it.

05:30.420 --> 05:32.200
Don't you think, Rimiya?

05:32.200 --> 05:34.210
What? I don't know.

05:34.210 --> 05:34.860
Huh?

05:35.820 --> 05:39.850
I was watching, but when the Mythic Beast 
pierced your shoulder with its whip,

05:39.850 --> 05:42.730
it looked like it was pumping 
something into you.

05:42.730 --> 05:45.370
And that's when the mana gauge got weird.

05:45.370 --> 05:46.530
What happened then?

05:47.460 --> 05:50.030
I saw a vision of monsters with wings.

05:51.480 --> 05:53.810
Was that mythic space?

05:53.810 --> 05:57.570
If so, then I wonder if those 
monsters were Shadow Angels.

06:00.200 --> 06:01.880
If only we could've held it together.

06:01.880 --> 06:03.630
That wasn't Rimiya-kun's fault!

06:03.630 --> 06:05.520
Huh? I didn't say it was—

06:09.750 --> 06:13.590
Rimiya-kun, don't pay any 
attention to Sakko here, okay?

06:13.940 --> 06:14.970
Okay.

06:15.800 --> 06:21.390
Uh, I mean, the teachers didn't say 
it was anybody's fault either.

06:22.040 --> 06:23.900
I'm going home.

06:24.880 --> 06:26.340
Rimiya-kun!

06:26.340 --> 06:27.170
Uh...

06:39.330 --> 06:43.340
Momohime

06:43.340 --> 06:46.640
It has already begun. 
The time of destruction is nigh!

06:46.630 --> 06:51.180
<b>Judgment Day Is Nigh</b>

06:46.630 --> 06:51.180
<b>Stop the Thirteenth
Universe Annihilation Project</b>

06:46.630 --> 06:51.180
<b>Large-Scale Disasters</b>

06:46.640 --> 06:47.760
Don't be deceived!

06:47.760 --> 06:50.850
The shadow world government 
is covering everything up!

06:53.150 --> 06:56.550
Ew! Kamisama's flyers are so sick!

06:56.800 --> 06:58.070
Who's Kamisama?

06:58.070 --> 07:01.060
That old guy who passes out flyers. 
That's what everyone calls him.

07:01.060 --> 07:02.830
I guess he does kind of seem like a god.

07:02.830 --> 07:04.180
Huh? How?

07:04.530 --> 07:06.210
Hey, Rimiya-kun, take a look at this.

07:06.210 --> 07:06.820
Huh?

07:06.820 --> 07:08.740
<b>Judgment Day Is Nigh</b>

07:06.820 --> 07:08.740
<b>Stop the Thirteenth
Universe Annihilation Project</b>

07:06.820 --> 07:08.740
<b>Large-Scale Disasters</b>

07:06.820 --> 07:08.740
Pandemics

07:06.820 --> 07:08.740
<b>They Are All</b>

07:06.820 --> 07:08.740
<b>a Plot by the
World Government!</b>

07:09.730 --> 07:12.210
Mm-hmm. I guess that sounds right.

07:12.210 --> 07:14.370
The world is full of sinister plots.

07:17.590 --> 07:20.000
Ta-da! Take a look, ladies and gentlemen.

07:20.000 --> 07:23.210
Your new unification simulator is here!

07:24.830 --> 07:28.470
Sensei, it looks just like the old one.

07:31.700 --> 07:37.260
Well, this machine measures your mana to 
simulate whether or not you can unite.

07:37.260 --> 07:38.890
Get it? Information is transmitted
 through your synapses

07:38.890 --> 07:40.260
by an ionic reaction of chemical substances.

07:40.260 --> 07:43.280
It resembles a quantum computing algorithm, 
which may produce irregularities,

07:43.280 --> 07:46.740
so I had to stay up all night with
 DEAVA figuring this out for you kids!

07:46.740 --> 07:48.970
There you have it! And if what's
 between your ears is that rotten anyway,

07:48.970 --> 07:50.540
you're gonna have to unite to—

07:54.180 --> 07:55.890
You need a sense of urgency!

08:00.800 --> 08:02.170
<i>Unify now!</i>

08:03.200 --> 08:03.960
Here we go.

08:04.220 --> 08:04.960
Yeah!

08:04.960 --> 08:06.050
Okay!

08:08.860 --> 08:10.000
Wha—?

08:10.000 --> 08:12.810
What the heck! I'm not feeling anything.

08:12.810 --> 08:14.980
Sensei, something is different.

08:14.980 --> 08:19.640
When we united before, we felt this, 
I don't know, something between us.

08:19.640 --> 08:22.980
<i>Sorry. I wasn't able to simulate that part.</i>

08:23.230 --> 08:27.430
<i>Next, let's change members. 
Tsukishiro-kun, trade places with Hatano-kun.</i>

08:27.430 --> 08:28.330
<i>All right.</i>

08:35.490 --> 08:36.780
<i>Unify now!</i>

08:36.780 --> 08:39.490
I'll do it this time. 
Ready, Sakko? Rimiya-kun?

08:39.490 --> 08:40.240
Yeah.

08:40.460 --> 08:41.480
Uh, yes.

08:46.890 --> 08:47.670
Hm?

08:49.740 --> 08:51.750
Not this again.

08:52.890 --> 08:56.040
Don't worry, Rimiya-kun. 
We'll just try again.

08:56.590 --> 08:58.240
Okay.

09:03.690 --> 09:05.300
Don't worry. Don't worry!

09:05.300 --> 09:06.630
I'm sorry.

09:07.450 --> 09:09.200
Let's just keep working at it.

09:09.200 --> 09:10.910
Momohime-senpai...

09:11.300 --> 09:14.750
Doesn't it seem like she's a 
little too nice to Rimiya-kun?

09:14.750 --> 09:17.030
Oh. You think so?

09:16.070 --> 09:19.680
Rimiya-kun, I know you're trying 
your hardest. It's okay. It's okay.

09:23.660 --> 09:25.160
Momohime

09:40.220 --> 09:44.310
<b>Where are you?
 Library
 I'm coming
 Wait for me
 Will do
 Did something happen today?
 You seemed kinda down</b>

09:54.820 --> 09:57.570
<b>Rimiya

Let's leave
 Where are you?
 Library
 I'm coming
 Wait for me
Got it</b>

10:00.750 --> 10:03.080
Momohime-senpai!

10:03.730 --> 10:04.730
Oh.

10:06.880 --> 10:07.960
Ah!

10:09.040 --> 10:11.040
<b>Nice to meet you!
 Let's kick butt in Element class!
 Nice to meet you as well!!
 I'll do my best!
 Hey! Are you free right now?
 Got time to meet?</b>

10:20.370 --> 10:21.660
Come over here.

10:26.080 --> 10:27.450
Um...

10:28.140 --> 10:30.250
Stars sure are mysterious.

10:30.250 --> 10:31.400
Huh?

10:31.410 --> 10:35.370
The stars we see are millions of years old,

10:35.370 --> 10:38.400
but we can only perceive that light now.

10:39.550 --> 10:40.580
Yeah...

10:51.750 --> 10:57.920
When we united, I felt emotions coming 
from both of you. It was really weird.

10:58.390 --> 11:00.670
But I don't mean it was gross.

11:00.670 --> 11:01.900
Oh?

11:01.900 --> 11:06.210
I'd just never felt anything 
like that before in my life.

11:07.410 --> 11:09.550
And it was really gentle.

11:10.490 --> 11:13.810
It felt like you really cared about me.

11:15.130 --> 11:17.400
Is that maybe what they call...

11:18.820 --> 11:21.410
I like you, Rimiya-kun.

11:21.620 --> 11:22.910
Huh?!

11:22.910 --> 11:25.150
I like Sakko and Toshi-kun too, of course.

11:27.280 --> 11:31.290
But I feel something with 
you that I don't with them.

11:33.290 --> 11:36.750
I've never fallen in love before.

11:36.750 --> 11:37.920
Uh...

11:37.920 --> 11:39.100
Huh?!

11:43.570 --> 11:45.620
Let's go on a date tomorrow!

11:47.190 --> 11:48.770
Ah!

11:48.990 --> 11:49.670
Oh...

11:54.370 --> 11:56.330
Rimiya-kun!

12:02.490 --> 12:05.180
G-Good morning, Momohime-senpai.

12:05.180 --> 12:06.490
Let's go, Rimiya-kun!

12:06.490 --> 12:07.600
Where to?

12:07.600 --> 12:08.540
This way! This way!

12:08.540 --> 12:09.490
By train?!

12:09.490 --> 12:12.730
Look. Wake up. Do not be fooled.

12:12.730 --> 12:15.890
All of humanity is under their control!

12:15.890 --> 12:18.030
That sounds like quite an interesting story.

12:18.030 --> 12:21.630
Why don't you tell us a 
little bit more about it?

12:28.080 --> 12:30.350
Ta-da! We're here!

12:32.710 --> 12:33.890
That wasn't far.

12:36.070 --> 12:38.040
I've always wanted to come here.

12:38.040 --> 12:40.580
Oh, you've never been here before?

12:40.580 --> 12:42.140
This is my first time.

12:42.140 --> 12:45.040
Even though you lived in 
Enoshima since primary school?

12:45.560 --> 12:48.400
I was never given a lot of freedom.

12:48.400 --> 12:49.400
How about you, Rimiya-kun?

12:49.640 --> 12:52.810
Yes, I've been here before. 
A girl I knew brought me here a bunch of times.

12:52.810 --> 12:55.110
Really? That sounds nice.

12:57.720 --> 13:00.250
Look, look! Wow!

13:06.010 --> 13:09.710
Oh, my gosh! Wow! Look, Rimiya-kun!

13:10.140 --> 13:11.610
Is she a child?

13:20.070 --> 13:21.590
It's really cute.

13:25.320 --> 13:27.730
Aren't you gonna go do parkour?

13:27.730 --> 13:30.150
What about you? 
Aren't you gonna study today?

13:30.430 --> 13:32.280
I have to take a break sometimes.

13:32.900 --> 13:34.060
So do I.

13:38.360 --> 13:43.460
I'm telling you, Momohime-senpai 
asked Rimiya-kun out on a date!

13:43.720 --> 13:45.530
Yeah. So what?

13:45.530 --> 13:47.470
What am I gonna do, Sakko?

13:47.470 --> 13:49.440
Who cares anyway?

13:51.880 --> 13:55.960
Momohime-senpai said she'd 
never been in love before.

13:55.960 --> 13:58.900
No kidding. Not with her personality.

13:58.900 --> 14:02.350
She said she wanted to confirm 
her feelings for Rimiya-kun.

14:02.350 --> 14:03.440
Huh...

14:05.270 --> 14:08.480
I wonder what they're doing right now.

14:14.830 --> 14:18.590
Momohime-senpai, why did you invite me out?

14:18.830 --> 14:23.760
Because the first time we met, it didn't 
feel like the first time, Rimiya-kun.

14:24.690 --> 14:29.360
I thought so, too! And I just 
couldn't stop thinking about you.

14:29.360 --> 14:30.480
Me neither!

14:31.570 --> 14:35.340
I'm sorry our union 
training didn't go well.

14:35.340 --> 14:38.660
I didn't realize until later that 
everyone thinks it's my fault.

14:38.660 --> 14:41.980
You're wrong!
All three of us were responsible.

14:42.820 --> 14:46.370
I still want to unite again.

14:49.350 --> 14:54.240
This reminds me. Sayo once told 
me a story about an eel god.

14:54.240 --> 14:55.120
Huh?

14:56.070 --> 14:59.290
She said the eel used 
to be king of the fish.

15:01.050 --> 15:05.700
There was once a beautiful girl named 
Ina who lived on the island of Mangaia.

15:05.700 --> 15:09.520
One day, when Ina was bathing in a pond,

15:09.520 --> 15:13.310
she caught the eye of Tuna, chief of 
the eels, who then began to court her.

15:13.800 --> 15:19.500
When Tuna bravely opened his heart to Ina, 
she accepted him, and the two were wed.

15:20.230 --> 15:26.110
However, when Tuna was forced to 
separate from Ina due to clan issues,

15:26.110 --> 15:29.320
he told her to cut off his head and bury it.

15:30.440 --> 15:32.600
Ina did exactly that,

15:33.050 --> 15:37.900
and two coconut trees grew out 
of the eel's buried head.

15:38.490 --> 15:41.640
Even today, it is said that when one takes 
the fruit of an island coconut tree,

15:41.640 --> 15:46.480
you can see the eyes and mouth 
of Ina's lover in the shell.

15:47.790 --> 15:48.880
Does that make sense?

15:48.880 --> 15:49.980
Huh?

15:49.980 --> 15:51.830
I wonder if that's what love is.

15:52.230 --> 15:54.960
No, I think that's different.

15:54.960 --> 16:00.380
I can't really understand those 
feelings. Neither Ina's nor Tuna's.

16:14.600 --> 16:16.280
Rimiya-kun, I apologize.

16:17.240 --> 16:21.710
Thanks to this date, I think I'm starting 
to understand my feelings a little better.

16:21.710 --> 16:23.010
Huh?

16:23.010 --> 16:25.000
These feelings I have for you...

16:25.670 --> 16:27.670
I don't think they're love.

16:29.470 --> 16:32.640
I think I'm starting to 
understand the thing I lack.

16:32.920 --> 16:35.020
Remember what the teacher said?

16:35.020 --> 16:39.090
That we were probably chosen to be 
Elements because we all lack something.

16:39.090 --> 16:43.340
So my feelings for you probably aren't—

16:43.340 --> 16:44.460
I agree!

16:44.460 --> 16:45.100
Huh?

16:45.850 --> 16:50.250
I have been in love before. 
Actually, ever since preschool...

16:50.250 --> 16:53.780
Ah, but as soon as we started going out, 
she wanted to break up.

16:53.780 --> 16:59.080
Well, that doesn't really matter, 
but I do know what it feels like to like a girl.

16:59.820 --> 17:00.780
And...

17:01.640 --> 17:07.030
And my feelings for you, Momohime-senpai, 
aren't like that at all.

17:07.350 --> 17:12.290
Like it isn't just love. Like it's 
more sacred than that, or something.

17:12.290 --> 17:13.650
Sacred...

17:21.450 --> 17:25.260
Sister, the lights in the 
fog glisten like stars!

17:27.100 --> 17:31.230
Be careful, Haida. The fog interferes 
with the transference of mana.

17:33.700 --> 17:37.610
It is told that on the night of the festival, 
the goddess's fog conceals the mana

17:37.610 --> 17:42.400
so that you will encounter the partner 
to whom you will promise your life!

17:42.400 --> 17:47.420
Then if we stay together like this, will that 
not end up obstructing your encounter?

17:47.650 --> 17:49.790
That is not why I...

17:49.790 --> 17:52.830
Oh, but I might obstruct 
yours as well, Sister.

17:54.800 --> 17:59.770
I too feel that as long as you stay with me,
I do not yet need a promised one.

18:01.010 --> 18:04.120
I do wonder how true the tale is, however.

18:05.010 --> 18:06.950
Shall we try going our separate 
ways for a while?

18:08.600 --> 18:09.650
Yes.

18:12.690 --> 18:13.860
Don't worry.

18:14.310 --> 18:18.830
Even without our mana connecting us, 
I can still find my little sister.

18:19.390 --> 18:24.160
Me, too. No matter where you 
go, Sister, I will find you.

18:25.650 --> 18:29.750
My beloved baby sister 
Haida, do not be sad.

18:30.280 --> 18:34.170
As a goddess, I will be able to 
watch over you for all time.

18:45.630 --> 18:46.530
Ooh!

18:53.060 --> 18:55.140
Rimiya-kun, you...

19:02.910 --> 19:03.800
Rimiya-kun!

19:03.800 --> 19:04.400
Right!

19:16.800 --> 19:17.960
We're here!

19:19.920 --> 19:22.100
C-Can you pilot, Rimiya?

19:22.670 --> 19:23.900
Of course!

19:22.670 --> 19:23.900
Of course!

19:27.360 --> 19:30.240
<i>Bridge catapult, launch sequence initiated.</i>

19:30.950 --> 19:33.040
<i>Vector Siegel, launching!</i>

19:34.140 --> 19:36.530
<i>Iwaya cave, launch sequence initiated.</i>

19:37.870 --> 19:40.130
<i>Vector Tir, launching!</i>

19:42.030 --> 19:45.320
<i>Yacht harbor, launch sequence initiated.</i>

19:45.320 --> 19:47.690
<i>Vector Feoh, launching!</i>

19:53.090 --> 19:56.210
<i>It's trying to expand its territory 
beyond the stake it placed.</i>

19:56.210 --> 19:58.020
<i>Don't let it near the city!</i>

19:58.020 --> 19:59.240
<i>Unite!</i>

20:00.930 --> 20:03.990
Mythic Star Union! Go, Aquarion!

20:25.830 --> 20:27.580
<i>Aquarion Feoh!</i>

20:29.670 --> 20:31.200
<i>Let's go, Rimiya-kun!</i>

20:31.200 --> 20:32.870
<i>Yes, Sister!</i>

20:32.870 --> 20:34.720
<i>Huh? Sis... What?</i>

21:01.860 --> 21:05.120
<i>Give me your strength, Rimiya-kun, Sakko!</i>

21:05.120 --> 21:05.870
<i>All right!</i>

21:05.120 --> 21:05.870
<i>All right!</i>

21:06.150 --> 21:07.320
<i>Aquarion</i>

21:07.750 --> 21:09.470
<i>Peach Special</i>

21:10.290 --> 21:11.740
<i>Dynamite!</i>

21:12.200 --> 21:14.160
<b>Peach Special Dynamite Strike</b>

21:23.230 --> 21:25.520
<i>What's a peach special?</i>

21:25.920 --> 21:30.370
<i>When Elements manifest their emotions in words,
they can draw upon their mana power</i>

21:30.370 --> 21:33.210
<i>to unleash one of Aquarion's 
special fighting moves!</i>

21:44.380 --> 21:48.780
Rimiya, we were worried about you.
Both me and Toshi.

21:49.170 --> 21:52.440
But he's okay now. Aren't you, Rimiya-kun?

21:52.440 --> 21:53.500
Yes!

21:55.770 --> 21:57.490
What's with you guys?

21:59.940 --> 22:02.310
An exchange student? This late in the year?

22:02.310 --> 22:05.480
Sounds like they were admitted 
directly into the Element class.

22:02.710 --> 22:05.970
<b>Enoshima Academy</b>
